# Backend & worker (NestJS)

## Module layout (`apps/backend/src/`)

```
modules/<feature>/
  <feature>.controller.ts   ← REST surface; thin; delegates to service
  <feature>.service.ts      ← business logic; pure where possible
  <feature>.module.ts
  dto/
    <action>.dto.ts          ← class-validator DTOs
  <feature>.service.spec.ts  ← unit (mock prisma + redis)
```

Integration tests live in `apps/backend/test/<feature>.e2e-spec.ts` (Testcontainers Postgres + Redis).

## Controllers

- Always specify HTTP verb + status decorator (`@Post()`, `@HttpCode(201)`).
- Always extract `playerId` from JWT via decorator (`@CurrentPlayer()`) — never trust body / query.
- DTOs are `class-validator` classes; reject extra fields with `forbidNonWhitelisted: true` (set globally).

```typescript
@Post()
@HttpCode(201)
async create(
  @CurrentPlayer() playerId: string,
  @Body() dto: BuildStationDto,
): Promise<StationDto> {
  return this.stations.build(playerId, dto);
}
```

## Authorization

Every mutation checks ownership in the service:

```typescript
async upgrade(playerId: string, id: string, dto: UpgradeStationDto) {
  const station = await this.prisma.station.findFirst({
    where: { id, playerId },         // 404 instead of 403 — no information leak
  });
  if (!station) throw new NotFoundException();
  // ...
}
```

## Transactions & locks

- Multi-row state changes (dispatch, completion, salary): single Prisma `$transaction`.
- Concurrent claims: Redis `SETNX` with PX TTL **before** opening the transaction (`engineering §6`).

## Rate limiting

Decorate or wrap action handlers with the shared rate limiter; limits per `engineering §10`. Auth endpoints return `429`; in-game actions emit `ACTION_REJECTED`.

## Worker tasks

- One scheduled job per file under `apps/worker/src/jobs/`.
- Acquire `lock:worker:<job>` (SETNX) before running — prevents duplicate ticks if multiple workers exist.
- Use `GameClockService` for any time-based logic; never inline `Date.now()` for game rules.

## Forbidden

- `console.log` (use injected `Logger`/pino).
- `prisma.$queryRawUnsafe` with interpolation.
- Returning the password hash, refresh token, or full JWT in any response.
- Mutations that don't go through `class-validator` DTOs.
